└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


keys:

    ctrl+t (or ctrl+n)      new shell tab
    ctrl+w                  close tab
    ctrl+→/← (or ctrl+f/b)  next / previous tab


install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash


update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash


make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`.
to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.


bundled development guardrails:

    tabs sync-rules --dry-run
    tabs sync-rules

syncs workflow-approval instructions into the global Claude, Codex and Pi
instruction files. they apply everywhere, not only inside tmux-tabs.
installation and updates automatically sync these instructions. launching
tabs does not rewrite them. the guardrails live in a separate bundled module
at `~/.local/share/tmux-tabs/guardrails.sh`.

"push" authorizes staging, committing and a normal push without repeated
consent questions. "make PR" also authorizes creating a PR; "push to PR"
creates one if missing. unrelated or destructive actions still need explicit
authorization. native tool/sandbox permission prompts are unchanged.

uses `~/.config/agents/AGENTS.md` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agents/AGENTS.md`)
when present, otherwise a bundled default. pass a file to use another policy:

    tabs sync-rules --dry-run path/to/policy.md
    tabs sync-rules path/to/policy.md

installation, updates and manual sync replace the managed TMUX-TABS SHARED
RULES section or legacy USER GIT APPROVAL RULES section automatically.
they do not wipe whole agent configs or try to remove unmarked custom rules;
review those yourself if they contradict the bundled policy.

preserves instructions outside its managed section and backs up each existing
file once as `<file>.before-tabs-rules`. honors CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME
and PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR. restart agents after syncing (or `/reload` in Pi).
